1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,600
Over the past month or so,

2
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:08,000
I think many people have been concerned about

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,760
the war between the U.S., Israel, and Iran —

4
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:14,000
a conflict that has shaken the global situation.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Today I'd like to start with this topic,

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,000
but from a different angle.

7
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,000
I think war serves as a kind of stage —

8
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:31,860
one where you can see how astonishing human invention can be.

9
00:00:31,860 --> 00:00:33,660
In this war,

10
00:00:33,660 --> 00:00:36,660
you can see all kinds of different weapons.

11
00:00:36,660 --> 00:00:39,660
I don't know if you've been following the news,

12
00:00:39,660 --> 00:00:41,660
but in the upper-left corner here,

13
00:00:41,660 --> 00:00:47,660
that's the MOAB — the Mother of All Bombs.

14
00:00:47,660 --> 00:00:54,660
It's the most powerful bomb in the conventional arsenal.

15
00:00:54,660 --> 00:00:59,660
Even just to drop it,

16
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:02,660
they need a C-130 Hercules transport plane,

17
00:01:02,660 --> 00:01:04,660
because it's too heavy and too large.

18
00:01:04,660 --> 00:01:07,660
This Mother of All Bombs

19
00:01:07,660 --> 00:01:09,160
is the strongest in the conventional category.

20
00:01:09,160 --> 00:01:12,660
If you want to go beyond that,

21
00:01:12,660 --> 00:01:15,660
you have to step into unconventional weapons —

22
00:01:15,660 --> 00:01:17,660
nuclear weapons, for example.

23
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:19,660
So this one is really pushing the limit.

24
00:01:19,660 --> 00:01:22,660
Next to it is the bunker-buster bomb.

25
00:01:22,660 --> 00:01:24,660
As you know, Iran has many

26
00:01:24,660 --> 00:01:27,660
underground missile cities,

27
00:01:27,660 --> 00:01:29,660
underground nuclear facilities.

28
00:01:29,660 --> 00:01:35,660
The bomber that drops these bunker busters is the B-2.

29
00:01:35,660 --> 00:01:38,660
The picture at the bottom left

30
00:01:38,660 --> 00:01:40,660
is a torpedo —

31
00:01:40,660 --> 00:01:47,660
a Mk 48 heavyweight torpedo.

32
00:01:47,660 --> 00:01:52,660
You might still remember, in the Indian Ocean,

33
00:01:52,660 --> 00:01:54,660
an Iranian frigate

34
00:01:54,660 --> 00:01:57,660
that had finished joint exercises with India

35
00:01:57,660 --> 00:01:58,660
was returning to Iran

36
00:01:58,660 --> 00:02:02,660
when it was sunk en route by a U.S. submarine.

37
00:02:02,660 --> 00:02:05,660
Honestly, that frigate wasn't a major warship,

38
00:02:05,660 --> 00:02:07,660
and it wasn't particularly advanced.

39
00:02:07,660 --> 00:02:10,660
A missile would have been enough to take it out.

40
00:02:10,660 --> 00:02:11,660
With a missile,

41
00:02:11,660 --> 00:02:14,660
you'd at least give the crew a chance to escape.

42
00:02:14,660 --> 00:02:17,660
But they actually used this heavy torpedo.

43
00:02:17,660 --> 00:02:20,660
If you watch the footage on YouTube,

44
00:02:20,660 --> 00:02:22,660
you'll see the ship went down very fast.

45
00:02:22,660 --> 00:02:23,660
Sri Lanka —

46
00:02:23,660 --> 00:02:26,660
by the time Sri Lanka's old vessels arrived,

47
00:02:26,660 --> 00:02:28,660
the ship had already sunk.

48
00:02:28,660 --> 00:02:35,660
Why use a heavyweight torpedo against it?

49
00:02:35,660 --> 00:02:39,660
The story is that on board the U.S. submarine that day —

50
00:02:39,660 --> 00:02:42,660
a Los Angeles-class sub —

51
00:02:42,660 --> 00:02:47,660
there were two Australian naval officers undergoing training.

52
00:02:47,660 --> 00:02:51,660
You know, Australia bought nuclear submarines from the U.S.,

53
00:02:51,660 --> 00:02:52,660
and in doing so,

54
00:02:52,660 --> 00:02:54,660
in a way they tacitly agreed

55
00:02:54,660 --> 00:02:57,660
that if anything happens at the first island chain in the Pacific,

56
00:02:57,660 --> 00:03:01,660
Australia would join the fight.

57
00:03:01,660 --> 00:03:04,660
So inside that submarine that day,

58
00:03:04,660 --> 00:03:08,660
it was effectively combat training as well.

59
00:03:08,660 --> 00:03:11,660
And next to it,

60
00:03:11,660 --> 00:03:13,660
another impressive one.

61
00:03:13,660 --> 00:03:16,660
That one is called the graphite bomb.

62
00:03:16,660 --> 00:03:18,660
They threatened —

63
00:03:18,660 --> 00:03:22,660
to bomb Iran's power plant with it.

64
00:03:22,660 --> 00:03:27,660
But notice — it's not the kind of weapon that harms civilians.

65
00:03:27,660 --> 00:03:29,660
Because they noticed one phenomenon:

66
00:03:29,660 --> 00:03:33,660
in some rural areas, in places with very few people,

67
00:03:33,660 --> 00:03:36,660
the electricity consumption was surprisingly high.

68
00:03:36,660 --> 00:03:39,660
That usually means there are nuclear facilities behind it,

69
00:03:39,660 --> 00:03:41,660
or maybe military installations.

70
00:03:41,660 --> 00:03:43,660
So the U.S. demand —

71
00:03:43,660 --> 00:03:47,660
their threat to bomb the power plant —

72
00:03:47,660 --> 00:03:50,660
but if you actually destroyed the plant, that would be terrible:

73
00:03:50,660 --> 00:03:52,660
it would affect many people and civilian life.

74
00:03:52,660 --> 00:03:54,660
So what is this graphite bomb?

75
00:03:54,660 --> 00:03:56,660
The moment it's deployed,

76
00:03:56,660 --> 00:04:00,660
the graphite itself causes massive short-circuits,

77
00:04:00,660 --> 00:04:02,660
which knocks out power transmission.

78
00:04:02,660 --> 00:04:04,660
But the power plant itself

79
00:04:04,660 --> 00:04:07,660
and the generating equipment are not destroyed.

80
00:04:07,660 --> 00:04:11,660
You can see — isn't that remarkable?

81
00:04:11,660 --> 00:04:15,660
Actually these kinds of warfare technologies —

82
00:04:15,660 --> 00:04:18,660
take U.S. drones, for example.

83
00:04:18,660 --> 00:04:20,660
The Lucas drone.

84
00:04:20,660 --> 00:04:22,660
Then there are unmanned speedboats, unmanned vessels.

85
00:04:22,660 --> 00:04:27,660
In the lower-left corner you can see one called Starshield.

86
00:04:27,660 --> 00:04:30,660
That's also from SpaceX.

87
00:04:30,660 --> 00:04:32,660
Starlink is for civilian use.

88
00:04:32,660 --> 00:04:35,660
Starshield is for military use.

89
00:04:35,660 --> 00:04:38,660
So if you take apart the nose cone of these drones,

90
00:04:38,660 --> 00:04:41,660
you'll find there are receivers inside,

91
00:04:41,660 --> 00:04:44,660
and those tap into Starshield for navigation.

92
00:04:44,660 --> 00:04:48,660
And in the upper-right corner,

93
00:04:48,660 --> 00:04:52,660
that one is a laser cannon.

94
00:04:52,660 --> 00:04:56,660
Actually, since around 2023,

95
00:04:56,660 --> 00:04:58,660
one thing that's become very popular

96
00:04:58,660 --> 00:05:00,660
is the so-called saturation attack.
